Tasks 2.1+2.2: Add Kafka producer resilience example

Summary: Mirrors ClientResilienceExampleSuite exactly, swapping purerest's
HTTP Resilience.middleware for purekafka's generic one, and a dummy Client[IO]
for a dummy (String, String) => IO[Unit] publish function. Added an
example-kafka-producer config block to application.conf (same shape/values as
example-client, not read by the live service). Two tests: transient-failure-
then-success (retried to success, 3 attempts), and sustained failure (circuit
breaker opens after a lowered threshold, third call rejected with
CircuitBreakerOpen before reaching the dummy publish function).

Also fixed a real giter8-escaping bug found along the way, and retroactively
applied the same fix convention to Task 1.2's amendment: a bare $n inside an
s-string (s"boom $n") is itself giter8 template syntax (an unmatched $
starts a property-name scan that can silently corrupt/truncate generation
with NO error reported by dev-regenerate.sh's own success check) - the fix is
the established convention already used throughout this template (e.g.
Migrations.scala, $domain_name;format="cap"$ServiceConfig.scala): escape as
\$n in the template source, which giter8 unescapes to plain $n in the
generated output, correctly interpolated there. Previously (Task 1.2's
amendment) I'd worked around an equivalent issue with string concatenation
instead of this escape - went back and converted that one to the same
convention for consistency, once the real mechanism was understood. Also
root-caused a separate, unrelated red herring during this investigation: a
leftover 'sbt run' process from Task 1.4's manual verification was never
actually killed (pkill -f "sbt run" didn't match it), and interfered with
later sbt invocations against the same regenerated directory - killed it
directly by PID once found.

